                        {
                          "id": "a88260e3-d29a-4703-b823-8ad92e16810a",
                          "text": "文档: `Not p`, or `¬p`, is the negation of `p`. It is defined to be `p → False`, so i…",
                          "children": [],
                          "isExpanded": true,
                          "parentId": "0807971b-e0ff-4291-b017-9133a162a4a4",
                          "data": {
                            "note": "**文档**\n\n`Not p`, or `¬p`, is the negation of `p`. It is defined to be `p → False`,\nso if your goal is `¬p` you can use `intro h` to turn the goal into\n`h : p ⊢ False`, and if you have `hn : ¬p` and `h : p` then `hn h : False`\nand `(hn h).elim` will prove anything.\nFor more information: [Propositional Logic](https://lean-lang.org/theorem_proving_in_lean4/propositions_and_proofs.html#propositional-logic)",
                            "tags": [
                              "attribute",
                              "文档"
                            ]
                          },
                          "style": {
                            "background": "#f9fafb",
                            "color": "#6b7280",
                            "fontSize": 11,
                            "borderColor": "#e5e7eb"
                          }
                        }
                      ],
                      "isExpanded": false,
                      "parentId": "a1206bdf-b5da-45e3-bfec-e0debe628985",
                      "data": {
                        "tags": [
                          "attribute-group"
                        ]
                      },
                      "style": {
                        "background": "#f3f4f6",
                        "color": "#4b5563",
                        "fontSize": 12,
                        "shape": "round",
                        "borderColor": "#d1d5db"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "8ec546e8-b120-4914-936d-0556198b3217",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 证明\n\n**类型** definition\n\n**模块** `Init.Prelude`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\nProp → Prop\n```\n\n**文档**\n`Not p`, or `¬p`, is the negation of `p`. It is defined to be `p → False`,\nso if your goal is `¬p` you can use `intro h` to turn the goal into\n`h : p ⊢ False`, and if you have `hn : ¬p` and `h : p` then `hn h : False`\nand `(hn h).elim` will prove anything.\nFor more information: [Propositional Logic](https://lean-lang.org/theorem_proving_in_lean4/propositions_and_proofs.html#propositional-logic)",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "证明",
                      "definition"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f7fef9",
                    "color": "#14532d",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#86efac"
                  }
