                        },
                        {
                          "id": "2e377e06-8b63-4f89-950e-f39be65cc505",
                          "text": "文档: A Boolean algebra is a bounded distributive lattice with a complement operator …",
                          "children": [],
                          "isExpanded": true,
                          "parentId": "1ceda38a-35da-460d-822a-9ddf977ab542",
                          "data": {
                            "note": "**文档**\n\nA Boolean algebra is a bounded distributive lattice with a complement operator `ᶜ` such that\n`x ⊓ xᶜ = ⊥` and `x ⊔ xᶜ = ⊤`. For convenience, it must also provide a set difference operation `\\`\nand a Heyting implication `⇨` satisfying `x \\ y = x ⊓ yᶜ` and `x ⇨ y = y ⊔ xᶜ`.\n\nThis is a generalization of (classical) logic of propositions, or the powerset lattice.\n\nSince `BoundedOrder`, `OrderBot`, and `OrderTop` are mixins that require `LE`\nto be present at define-time, the `extends` mechanism does not work with them.\nInstead, we extend using the underlying `Bot` and `Top` data typeclasses, and replicate the\norder axioms of those classes here. A \"forgetful\" instance back to `BoundedOrder` is provided.",
                            "tags": [
                              "attribute",
                              "文档"
                            ]
                          },
                          "style": {
                            "background": "#f9fafb",
                            "color": "#6b7280",
                            "fontSize": 11,
                            "borderColor": "#e5e7eb"
                          }
                        }
                      ],
                      "isExpanded": false,
                      "parentId": "58b6c378-f2b1-4eb2-8906-fa6d89bfc7e3",
                      "data": {
                        "tags": [
                          "attribute-group"
                        ]
                      },
                      "style": {
                        "background": "#f3f4f6",
                        "color": "#4b5563",
                        "fontSize": 12,
                        "shape": "round",
                        "borderColor": "#d1d5db"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "2facfede-bb79-4e05-9ac9-4060d1fff233",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 证明\n\n**类型** inductive\n\n**模块** `Mathlib.Order.BooleanAlgebra.Defs`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\nType u → Type u\n```\n\n**文档**\nA Boolean algebra is a bounded distributive lattice with a complement operator `ᶜ` such that\n`x ⊓ xᶜ = ⊥` and `x ⊔ xᶜ = ⊤`. For convenience, it must also provide a set difference operation `\\`\nand a Heyting implication `⇨` satisfying `x \\ y = x ⊓ yᶜ` and `x ⇨ y = y ⊔ xᶜ`.\n\nThis is a generalization of (classical) logic of propositions, or the powerset lattice.\n\nSince `BoundedOrder`, `OrderBot`, and `OrderTop` are mixins that require `LE`\nto be present at define-time, the `extends` mechanism does not work with them.\nInstead, we extend using the underlying `Bot` and `Top` data typeclasses, and replicate the\norder axioms of those classes here. A \"forgetful\" instance back to `BoundedOrder` is provided.",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "证明",
                      "inductive"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f7fef9",
                    "color": "#14532d",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#86efac"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "3c8207d4-4b8e-4a6f-9894-e1b23a4a9ada",
                  "text": "[证明] BooleanAlgebra.mk",
